Title: "`mlg structure`"
Id: "8540a911-39db-4876-b605-6453d10ab285"

Text: "`mlg structure` inspects the collection layout, table of contents, and items hierarchy.

```text
mlg structure [--json]
```

In default human-readable mode, it prints the collection title, the discovered directory hierarchy (including whether each directory has a preface), each file's title and defined commands, and the individual items in each file with their UUIDs, kinds, headings, and definition keys.

With `--json`, `mlg structure` emits a structured JSON object representing the entire collection hierarchy:

```text
{
  \"title\": \"Collection Title\",
  \"directories\": [
    {
      \"path\": \"content/path\",
      \"title\": \"Section Title\",
      \"hasPreface\": true
    }
  ],
  \"files\": [
    {
      \"path\": \"content/path/file.mlg\",
      \"title\": \"Page Title\",
      \"definedCommands\": [\"\\command.name\"],
      \"items\": [
        {
          \"id\": \"uuid-here\",
          \"kind\": \"Theorem\",
          \"heading\": \"\\theorem.name\",
          \"definitionKeys\": [\"\\theorem.name\"],
          \"commands\": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

The command accepts the global event filters: `--event-audience` (or `--event-scope`), `--event-level`, and `--event-markers`."
Id: "f6b3e812-2591-4cf1-884e-28ec3ca9942a"
